        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF149 adds support for additional characters to be allowed in attribute and element names in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1773312\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1773312</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Previously  you could only use the chars allowed in XML names - now the rules are less restrictive to allow the same chars as the HTML parser.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Spec update: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1263558481\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/7991\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/html/pull/7991/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/7991\">whatwg/html#7991</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome states support in 143:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/chrome-143-beta#allow_more_characters_in_javascript_dom_apis\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/chrome-143-beta#allow_more_characters_in_javascript_dom_apis</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6278918763708416\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6278918763708416</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Webkit added support in <a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=241419\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=241419</a>  but I don't think this made it to Safari yet.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3978124831\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43218\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43218/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43218\">mdn/content#43218</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29217",
            "title": "Chrome 143 / Firefox 149 allow more characters in DOM APIs",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-03T13:02:08.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-10T04:29:38.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 144 supports the <code class=\"notranslate\">::search-text</code> pseudo-element, which allows custom styling to be applied to browser search results; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5195073796177920\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5195073796177920</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">We already have BCD for <code class=\"notranslate\">::search-text</code>, however, you can combine <code class=\"notranslate\">::search-text</code> with the <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> pseudo-class to style the currently-highlighted search term on the page. This currently doesn't have any BCD, so I am using this PR to add <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> BCD.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm assuming it makes sense to put Chrome 144 down for this as well, as previously, there was no context in which <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> was supported. However, you might have other opinions on this.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I also thought about putting <code class=\"notranslate\">\"partial_implementation\": \"true\"</code> for this, but then again, <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> is fully supported in the context it is supported in. It just isn't supported in other contexts.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28882",
            "title": "Chrome 144 :current support",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-03T12:43:28.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-21T18:28:23.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There is updates to add details to cover Safari support for documentId and parentDocumentId. More information on changes see the related content PR. (TBC)</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #28341.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3575616610\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28341\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28341/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28341\">#28341</a><br>\nRelated content changes in (TBC)</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28790",
            "title": "Issue-28341 webextension.api documentId and parentDocumentId updates",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-15T15:37:17.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-09T18:11:24.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5876799?u=82c90e0406d442472b9120fe35a16b192fddd7d1&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>lists Safari 26 (and mirrored iOS and WebView) as removing support for <code class=\"notranslate\">html.elements.meta.name.theme-color</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test Results and Supporting Details</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/andesco/Safari-color-tinting\">https://github.com/andesco/Safari-color-tinting</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://safari-color-tinting.pages.dev\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://safari-color-tinting.pages.dev</a></li>\n</ul>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28503",
            "title": "Safari 26 uses `<meta name=\"theme-color\">` only for web apps",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-12T13:12:06.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-21T20:01:18.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "andesco",
                "url": "https://github.com/andesco"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Unmarks Firefox as partial for <code class=\"notranslate\">::highlight</code> CSS Selector, and splits up the existing notes, adding bug links.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I challenge the following <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/tree/main/docs/data-guidelines#partial_implementation-general-usage-guidelines\">requirement for partial implementation</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The browser's support has a demonstrable negative impact on web developers.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3586286163\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28374\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28374/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28374\">#28374</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28375",
            "title": "Unmark Firefox as partial for `::highlight` CSS selector",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-09T14:46:13.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-04T12:12:56.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chromium browsers support <a href=\"https://privacysandbox.google.com/protections/user-agent\" rel=\"nofollow\">User-Agent reduction</a>, which means that features such as the <code class=\"notranslate\">User-Agent</code> HTTP header provide less-specific information in an effort to reduce their effectiveness for fingerprinting/tracking.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds data points covering User-Agent reduction to relevant web platform features that I know to be affected by the change.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Compat data sources:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>From looking at <a href=\"https://blog.chromium.org/2021/09/user-agent-reduction-origin-trial-and-dates.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://blog.chromium.org/2021/09/user-agent-reduction-origin-trial-and-dates.html</a>, it looks like rollout of UA reduction to 100% of Chromium desktop users occurred in version 110, while the version was 113 for Chromium Android users. I asked <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/miketaylr/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/miketaylr\">@miketaylr</a> about this, and he confirmed it to be correct.</li>\n<li>From looking at <a href=\"https://www.chromium.org/updates/ua-reduction/#applicable-platforms\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.chromium.org/updates/ua-reduction/#applicable-platforms</a>, it looks like Android WebView should be <code class=\"notranslate\">false</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Another question for Mike: For all of these data points, I used <a href=\"https://wicg.github.io/ua-client-hints/#user-agent\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wicg.github.io/ua-client-hints/#user-agent</a> as the <code class=\"notranslate\">spec_url</code>. Are there better spec URLs we can point to for these individual features?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR is part of the final set of privacy sandbox information to be added to MDN. Much of it is being removed, but this feature is stable and will be kept, so it should be added.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28275",
            "title": "Chrome 110 applies User-Agent reduction to Navigator properties + `User-Agent` header",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-10T11:03:32.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-23T15:21:08.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43868318?u=3f179cacfd70db40ae7c11f1b951533a8ebf45bf&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Added caret.json with compatibility data structure</li>\n<li>Currently no browser support, but Chrome support expected soon</li>\n<li>Marked as experimental and standard track</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27904",
            "title": "Add CSS caret property (WIP - awaiting browser support)",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-16T16:55:16.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-16T16:54:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "yashrajbharti",
                "url": "https://github.com/yashrajbharti"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/644927?u=790461985bc61a38ef27bed89be1fdec9ace7cbc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Safari 14.1 and newer displays a time picker for <code class=\"notranslate\">datetime-local</code>.<br>\n<code class=\"notranslate\">datetime-local</code> was not working correctly in one of the Safari tech previews but was fixed before the final 14.1 release.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See the Safari 14.1 release note (<a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/safari-release-notes/safari-14_1-release-notes\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.apple.com/documentation/safari-release-notes/safari-14_1-release-notes</a>)</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Added support for HTML date, time, and datetime-local input types in macOS, enabling date and time controls in forms.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is confirmed by the according issue (comment 27): <a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=214946#c27\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=214946#c27</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">More confirmations:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>With screenshot: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"717735603\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/Fyrd/caniuse/issues/5646\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/Fyrd/caniuse/pull/5646/hovercard?comment_id=715180664&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/Fyrd/caniuse/pull/5646#issuecomment-715180664\">Fyrd/caniuse#5646 (comment)</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"728444766\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/Fyrd/caniuse/issues/5669\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/Fyrd/caniuse/pull/5669/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/Fyrd/caniuse/pull/5669\">Fyrd/caniuse#5669</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">A jsfiddle to test yourself: <a href=\"https://jsfiddle.net/8gw2yk5e/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://jsfiddle.net/8gw2yk5e/</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=214946#c27\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=214946#c27</a> (see comment 27)</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27762",
            "title": "Remove note about Safari time picker for `datetime-local`",
